From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: AV1 video decoders (Main, 8- and 10-bit)

D3D11VA AV1 profile 0 decoders on Vulkan Video (VK_KHR_video_decode_av1),
NV12 and P010 output from one decoder profile (a profile may now have
more than one output format). DXVA_PicParams_AV1 gives the frame header
and what of the sequence header the decoder needs; what DXVA does not
repeat -- each reference's order hint, its own references' order hints,
its frame type, sign bias and CDF/segmentation flags -- is kept per DPB
slot from that reference's own decode, and skip mode's references are
worked out from the order hints as the AV1 specification does. Tiles come
from DXVA_Tile_AV1, their offsets into the bitstream buffer as Vulkan
takes them. Film grain is not applied (the DPB and the output are one
picture); a stream asking for it is decoded without it, with one warning.

Offered only where proven (d3d11.videoDecode): bit-exact against dav1d
on NVIDIA's driver (libaom 8/10-bit, tiles, loop restoration; SVT-AV1
10-bit with hidden frames).
